==Speed Up==
{| class="article-table" border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 600px;"
|[[File:GatyaitemD 00 f 01.png|center]]
|'''English Version:''' Doubles your Battle speed.<br>[[Battle Cats Officers' Club|Gold Card Officers]] receive 3x battle speed!<br>(Tap icon to toggle ON/OFF during battle.)<br>
'''Japanese Version:''' 戦闘スピードが2倍速になります<br>戦闘中アイテムをタップすれば<br>ON・OFFが可能
|}
*'''Cost:''' '''50''' Cat Food ('''25''' during a sale) for '''9''' items | '''Nintendo Switch Cost''': '''25''' Cat Food for '''2''' items | '''Nintendo 3DS Cost:''' '''1''' Cat Food for '''1''' item
*'''Usage:''' A Speed Up can be activated or deactivated at any time, and does what the description says - Everything happens in battle twice as fast (including [[Timed Score Reward|timed score]] depletion, movement speeds, recharge rates, spawn frequencies and attacks, but not [[The Cat God (Special Cat)|Cat God]]'s Baby Boom Miracle timer, which scales on real time and counts down at the same speed even if Speed Up is in effect), however it can be used to beat long stages like [[Absolute Defense (Insane)|Absolute Defence]] or [[Flappy Cat (Insane)|Flappy Cat]] faster, or just to grind faster. Note that after [[Version 8.4 Update|Version 8.4]], Speed Ups are the only battle items that carry over to [[Continuation Stage]]s.
*Starting from [[Version 15.4 Update]], Speed Ups are provided in unlimited quantities. They will always be available in battles even if not used prior to entering one, though they won't begin automatically enabled. The player can also activate a triple speed multiplier by tapping the Speed Up icon twice, which comes at the cost of one Speed Up item unless they have the [[Officers' Club]] Gold Pass.
*'''Obtained:''' [[Tuesday Stage]] or [[Speed Cat (Veteran)|Tuesday Blitz Stage]].

==Treasure Radar==
{| class="article-table" border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 600px;"
|[[File:GatyaitemD 01 f.png|center]]
|'''English Version:''' 100% reward drop rate upon a Victory in battle.<br>Guaranteed to receive Superior [[Treasure]]<br>or Cat Unit, or XP/Catfruit stage drop reward.<br>
'''Japanese Version:''' お宝出現率アップ！<br>勝利すれば100％の確率で<br>最高のお宝をゲットすることができる
|}
*'''Cost:''' '''90''' Cat Food ('''45''' during a sale) for '''2''' items | '''Nintendo Switch Cost''': '''45''' Cat Food for '''2''' items | '''Nintendo 3DS Cost:''' '''3''' Cat Food for '''1''' item
*'''Usage:''' Treasure Radar should be used for getting the 30% legend drops ([[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]], etc), as well as [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent]] stages, to avoid having to redo such difficult stages for an otherwise elusive reward. Their use is further advised on [[Taste of Success (Merciless)|Merciless XP]] and [[Archfiend's Temptation]] to get extremely high XP drop rewards; otherwise do not use them for [[:Category:XP Guerrilla Stages|XP Guerrilla Stages]]. These items are extremely valuable because there is no weekly stage for it - hence, usage on most other stages are inadvisable, and you should experiment with your strategy until it could comfortably clear the stage. [[Cat Capsule#Lucky Capsules|Lucky Ticket]] stages and occasional events are the best way to obtain these. Using a Treasure Radar on an invalid stage (such as those lacking rewards in the first place or already had their rewards claimed) will instead reward another copy of itself on stage clear, effectively refunding it.

==Rich Cat==
{| class="article-table" border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 600px;"
|[[File:GatyaitemD 02 f.png|center]]
|'''English Version:''' [[Worker Cat]] starts the battle at MAX Level.<br>Seize the advantage in battle without needing<br>to spend money on upgrading Worker Cat!<br>
'''Japanese Version:''' 戦闘開始時から働きネコのレベルが<br>MAX状態でスタートします
|}
*'''Cost:''' '''150''' Cat Food ('''75''' during a sale) for '''7''' items | '''Nintendo Switch Cost''': '''75''' Cat Food for '''7''' items | '''Nintendo 3DS Cost''': '''2''' Cat Food for '''1''' item
*'''Usage:''' The Rich Cat is very effective in hard stages; the player can save money for expensive Cat Units, instead of spending funds on quickly upgrading the [[Worker Cat]]. Additionally, since Worker Cat starts at max level, money generation is faster, which is especially useful on rush stages and cheese strats. It is not useful in stages where you can stall easily since you would be able to upgrade the Worker Cat eventually. The Rich Cat is most effective when used on short stages or stages with a really difficult start. Has priority over Worker Start Level UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] and will override their effects.
*'''Obtained: '''[[Monday Stage]] or [[Rich Cat (Veteran)|Monday Blitz Stage]].

==Cat CPU==
{| class="article-table" border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 600px;"
|[[File:GatyaitemD 03 f.png|center]]
|'''English Version:''' Leave the battle to the Cat CPU!<br>It's only useful to a point, having been<br>programmed by mere Cats, but it's just advanced enough<br>to handle stages you've previously cleared.
'''Japanese Version:''' ネコ型CPUが戦闘をやってくれます<br>ネコ型なので性能は期待できない<br>アイコンを追加タップすると性能が超アップして<br>「Clear!」ステージの戦闘をスキップできます
|}
*'''Cost:''' '''180''' Cat Food ('''90''' during a sale) for '''20''' items| '''Nintendo Switch Cost''': '''90''' Cat Food for '''20''' items | '''Nintendo 3DS Cost''': '''1''' Cat Food for '''1''' item
*'''Usage:''' The player can use this item to spawn units immediately when their recharge is complete, which is useful when the player needs to meatshield for a long time, or spam many units, such as on [[Wrath of the Dogelord (Merciless)|Wrath of the Dogelord]] and [[Absolute Defense (Insane)|Absolute Defence]]. Because of its expensive nature, it only works if your economy is going well. The CPU can be activated or disengaged at will. Another unlisted effect is that it will fire the cat cannon automatically, which can become a serious hazard if it needs to be saved for something else.
*Starting from [[Version 12.5 Update|Version 12.5]], after beating [[Hawaii (Empire of Cats)|Hawaii]] in [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 1, tapping the Cat CPU twice will turn it golden. The golden CPU can instantly clear most stages, along with granting any [[Treasure]] or drop rewards, and can even be used with Treasure Radar/Cat Jobs to grant their effects as well, saving the player time and effort for particularly difficult stages, such as [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]]. This feature will consume two Cat CPUs or one if the player have [[Officers' Club]] Gold Pass, and can be used up to ten times per day. Tapping the Cat CPU again while it is golden turns it off again.
**Stages that cannot be skipped by the golden CPU include: stages that haven't been cleared or have been reset, [[Catclaw Dojo]], [[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]], [[Underground Labyrinth]], [[Mining Epic]], and [[Growing Evil]]. Stages that do not yield the default "You cannot skip battles you have not cleared yet" message will instead respond with "No skipping battles fur this stage! Meows the time to fight with your own strength!"
**Because the player doesn't actually enter battle and does not require a formation, any Cat Combos (such as [[Good Jobs! (Combo)|Good Jobs!]]) have no effect.
**The golden CPU will not increase the [[Timed Score Reward|Timed Score]] on any stages it clears, and will not allow access to a [[Continuation Stage]].
*'''Obtained:''' [[Friday Stage]] or [[Helpful Cat (Veteran)|Friday Blitz Stage]].

