*'''Usage:''' This item is very effective in stages with already high XP rewards on clear, such as [[XP Stage]] or [[Refined Palate (Insane)|XP Megablitz]]. This does not affect XP obtained as item drop rewards. This item is extremely useful in [[Tempered in Flame (Deadly)|XP Colosseum]], [[Taste of Success (Merciless)|Merciless XP]] and [[Archfiend's Temptation]], but doesn't have any value elsewhere.
*'''Obtained:''' [[Wednesday Stage]] or [[Cat Jobs (Veteran)|Wednesday Blitz Stage]].

==Sniper the Cat==
{| class="article-table" border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 600px;"
|[[File:GatyaitemD 05 f.png|center]]
|'''English Version:''' Pushes back enemies with cover fire. Attack<br>power changes dependent on [[Cat Base]] health.<br>(Tap icon to toggle ON/OFF during battle.)<br>
'''Japanese Version:''' スナイパーが援護射撃をしてくれます<br>弾が当たると必ずヒットバック<br>攻撃力は城の体力に比例します
|}
*'''Cost:''' '''90''' Cat Food ('''45''' during a sale) for '''3''' items | '''Nintendo Switch Cost''': '''45''' Cat Food for '''3''' items | '''Nintendo 3DS Cost: 2''' Cat Food for '''1''' item
*'''Usage:''' Sniper the Cat fires a [[Single Attack]] projectile once every 10 seconds that deals 5% of the [[Cat Base]]'s maximum health in damage to the closest enemy with an active hitbox. On a successful hit, the bullet will force the enemy to flinch, pushing them back by 55 distance, also making their hitbox inactive for 11f and causing their attack animation to be reset. However, if you disable Sniper the Cat during his firing animation (before the projectile lands), the timer will reset to 0 and you will have to wait 10 seconds for another shot. Sniper the Cat can be enabled or disabled during battle by tapping on the icon in the top right, Sniper the Cat has about 7f delay between activation time and deactivation time. Disabling Sniper will pause his 10 second attack timer. This knockback effect is identical to the one caused by the default Cat Cannon and any Zombies hit by Holy Blast but distinct from Knockback effects caused by Breakerblast and other sources of that effect, meaning [[:Category:Enemies with Knockback Immunity|Knockback Immune]] enemies are vulnerable, and [[Sage Enemies]] are not resistant to it, although [[Barrier]]s and [[Shield]]s will still block this effect, and it will be overridden if its damage triggers a stagger. Sniper can't harm the [[Enemy Bases|enemy base]], but is capable of engaging enemies that are behind them.
*'''Obtained:''' [[Thursday Stage]] or [[Sniper Cat (Veteran)|Thursday Blitz Stage]].

