==Trivia==
*Cat Jobs, Rich Cat and Sniper the Cat all have [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] counterparts added in [[Version 4.4 Update|Version 4.4]]: [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Freshman Cat Jobs]], [[Rich Cat III (Super Rare Cat)|Rich Cat III]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]].
*Rich Cat's Japanese name, Nekobon (ネコボン), is derived from 猫 ''neko'' (cat) and ボンボン ''bonbon'' (rich young man from a wealthy family).
*Rich Cat III is Rich Cat's heir (cousin in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]]), Rich Cat Sr. is Rich Cat's father, and Richest Cat is Rich Cat's grandfather.
*Some of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] are "Cat Jobs will guide you to success!" and "You'll become smarter than a Cat CPU!"
*In the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]], the Cat CPU still uses its old description when viewed from the Item Store.
*The Nintendo Switch and Nintendo 3DS versions still contain the old version of the Speed Up battle item in which it only has a max 2x speed multiplier and lacks thereof the 3x speed multiplier.

